part e1_asks_03
  tally 2
  note "E1-03 · Gifts and inheritances (tmp/cases/E1/questions.md): as of and known 2025-12-31. The tax on Zbigniew's estate for Anna, Piotr and Jakub turns on whether each reported by d.report_by, which no paper states: here it is a hole naming that, and each case states D's rows reported_on for the three: e1_03_reported pins them (L §5.18: in a joint model a value pin may name a member's row), each reported on d.report_by; e1_03_not_reported reads the scenario e1_not_reported (scenarios/e1_not_reported.tally), none reported. Halina's gifts to Ania are A's acquisitions from Halina to Ania, a binding over A's index acq (e1_03_givers shows every acquisition's giver and acquirer)."

ask e1_03_anna_from_halina: a.gift_tax[g] for g in a.acq where a.acq_from[g] == halina and a.acq_to[g] == a.ania law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_anna_from_halina_sum: sum(a.gift_tax[g] for g in a.acq where a.acq_from[g] == halina and a.acq_to[g] == a.ania) law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_dates: d.igt_arises, d.report_by law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_gifts_in_estate: e1_gifts_in_estate law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_givers: a.acq_from[g], a.acq_to[g] for g in a.acq law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_halina: d.reported_on[halina], d.igt_tax[halina] law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_heirs: d.igt_tax[h] for h in [anna, piotr, jakub] law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_not_reported: d.igt_tax[h] for h in [anna, piotr, jakub] in e1_not_reported law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31

ask e1_03_reported: d.igt_tax[h] for h in [anna, piotr, jakub] with d.reported_on[anna] = d.report_by, d.reported_on[piotr] = d.report_by, d.reported_on[jakub] = d.report_by law 2025-12-31 as known 2025-12-31
